[2025-10-20T19:25:28Z INFO  ai_agent_audit::llm_review::phases::add_poc_findings] AI Agent: This PoC demonstrates how rounding dust from the 80/20 split in PuppyRaffle.selectWinner permanently locks protocol fees. The test uses an entrance fee of 1 wei (not divisible by 5) and enters 4 players, creating a total pot of 4 wei. When selectWinner is called, the prize pool calculation (4*80/100) results in 3 wei, while the fee calculation (4*20/100) results in 0 wei due to integer division rounding down. This leaves 1 wei of dust in the contract. Since the withdrawFees function requires address(this).balance == totalFees, and totalFees is 0 while the contract balance is 1, the withdrawal function will always revert. The test shows this is permanent by running another raffle cycle, which only adds more dust to the contract.
